                <h2><a href=3D"https://stochasticfractals.wordpress.com/200=
9/05/05/standard-deviation-of-fractional-brownian-motion/">Standard Deviati=
on of Fractional Brownian&nbsp;Motion</a></h2>

                <p>Let <img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3DB_%7=
BH%7D%28t%29&amp;bg=3De6e6e6&amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" al=
t=3D"B_{H}(t)" class=3D"latex"> be the zero-mean Fractional Brownian Motion=
 process of Hurst parameter <img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=
=3DH+%280+%5Cle+H+%5Cle+1%29&amp;bg=3De6e6e6&amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;=
c=3D20201002" alt=3D"H (0 \le H \le 1)" class=3D"latex">, such a process is=
 defined as having the following covariance structure:</p>
<p><img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3DE%5BB_%7BH%7D%28t%29B_%7=
BH%7D%28s%29%5D%3D%5Cfrac%7B1%7D%7B2%7D%28%7Ct%7C%5E%7B2H%7D%2B%7Cs%7C%5E%7=
B2H%7D-%7Ct-s%7C%5E%7B2H%7D%29&amp;bg=3De6e6e6&amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&am=
p;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"E[B_{H}(t)B_{H}(s)]=3D\frac{1}{2}(|t|^{2H}+|s|^{2H}-=
|t-s|^{2H})" class=3D"latex">  (1)</p>
<p>Then(by taking s=3Dt in (1))</p>
<p><img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3DVar%28B_%7BH%7D%28t%29%2=
9%3DE%5B%28B_%7BH%7D%28t%29-E%28B_%7BH%7D%28t%29%29%29%5E2%5D%3DE%5BB_%7BH%=
7D%5E%7B2%7D%28t%29%5D%3D%7Ct%7C%5E%7B2H%7D&amp;bg=3De6e6e6&amp;fg=3D333333=
&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"Var(B_{H}(t))=3DE[(B_{H}(t)-E(B_{H}(t))=
)^2]=3DE[B_{H}^{2}(t)]=3D|t|^{2H}" class=3D"latex"></p>
<p>Which gives the standard deviation as <img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/late=
x.php?latex=3D%7Ct%7C%5EH&amp;bg=3De6e6e6&amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=
=3D20201002" alt=3D"|t|^H" class=3D"latex"> (and for the Wiener Brownian Mo=
tion, we indeed get a standard deviation of <img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/l=
atex.php?latex=3D%5Csqrt%7Bt%7D&amp;bg=3De6e6e6&amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&a=
mp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"\sqrt{t}" class=3D"latex">)</p>
			=09
                <p class=3D"meta">

                <span class=3D"date"><a href=3D"https://stochasticfractals.=
wordpress.com/2009/05/05/">May 5, 2009</a> <!-- at 2:22 pm --></span>

								<span class=3D"postedby">
                  Posted by               	  <a href=3D"https://stochasticf=
ractals.wordpress.com/author/jppoton/" rel=3D"author">Jean-Philippe</a> |
                  <a href=3D"https://stochasticfractals.wordpress.com/categ=
ory/fractional-brownian-motion/" rel=3D"category tag">Fractional Brownian M=
otion</a>				   |
                  <a href=3D"https://stochasticfractals.wordpress.com/2009/=
05/05/standard-deviation-of-fractional-brownian-motion/#respond">Leave a co=
mment</a>                  								</span>

             	</p>

