                <h2><a href=3D"https://stochasticfractals.wordpress.com/200=
9/05/04/maximum-of-wiener-brownian-motion/">Maximum of Wiener Brownian&nbsp=
;Motion</a></h2>

                <p style=3D"text-align:left;">Let <img src=3D"https://s0.wp=
.com/latex.php?latex=3DW_0&amp;bg=3De6e6e6&amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=
=3D20201002" alt=3D"W_0" class=3D"latex"> be the standard Wiener Brownian M=
otion process, and <img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3DM%28t%29=
&amp;bg=3De6e6e6&amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"M(t)" c=
lass=3D"latex"> defined as <img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3D=
M%28t%29%3D%5Cmax_%7B0+%5Cleq+s+%5Cleq+t%7D+W_%7B0%7D%28t%29&amp;bg=3De6e6e=
6&amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"M(t)=3D\max_{0 \leq s =
\leq t} W_{0}(t)" class=3D"latex">, we then have the following result:</p>
<p><img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3DP%28M%28t%29+%5Cgeq+x%29=
%3D+2%281-%5Cphi%28%5Cfrac%7Bx%7D%7B%5Csqrt%7Bt%7D%7D%29%29&amp;bg=3De6e6e6=
&amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"P(M(t) \geq x)=3D 2(1-\=
phi(\frac{x}{\sqrt{t}}))" class=3D"latex"></p>
<p>where <img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3D%5Cphi&amp;bg=3De6=
e6e6&amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"\phi" class=3D"late=
x"> denotes the standard normal cumulative distribution function:</p>
<p><img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3D%5Cphi%28z%29%3D%5Cfrac%=
7B1%7D%7B%5Csqrt%7B2%5Cpi%7D%7De%5E%7B-z%5E%7B2%7D%2F2%7D&amp;bg=3De6e6e6&a=
mp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"\phi(z)=3D\frac{1}{\sqrt{=
2\pi}}e^{-z^{2}/2}" class=3D"latex">    <img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex=
.php?latex=3D%5Cforall%7Bz%7D%5Cin%5Cmathbb%7BR%7D&amp;bg=3De6e6e6&amp;fg=
=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"\forall{z}\in\mathbb{R}" class=
=3D"latex"> </p>
<p>This result is simply a direct application of Theorem 2 from <a href=3D"=
http://www.stat.purdue.edu/research/technical_reports/pdfs/1988/tr88-40.pdf=
">this paper</a> with <img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3D%5Cal=
pha%3D0&amp;bg=3De6e6e6&amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"=
\alpha=3D0" class=3D"latex"></p>
			=09
                <p class=3D"meta">

                <span class=3D"date"><a href=3D"https://stochasticfractals.=
wordpress.com/2009/05/04/">May 4, 2009</a> <!-- at 4:40 pm --></span>

								<span class=3D"postedby">
                  Posted by               	  <a href=3D"https://stochasticf=
ractals.wordpress.com/author/jppoton/" rel=3D"author">Jean-Philippe</a> |
                  <a href=3D"https://stochasticfractals.wordpress.com/categ=
ory/wiener-brownian-motion/" rel=3D"category tag">Wiener Brownian Motion</a=
>				   |
                  <a href=3D"https://stochasticfractals.wordpress.com/2009/=
05/04/maximum-of-wiener-brownian-motion/#respond">Leave a comment</a>      =
            								</span>

             	</p>

